{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791595864,"nonce":"rjA3oLcLOsvJWc+F8gxnVbRJVKs=","title":"Liquid glass on a concave-top notch shows a bright sliver along the top edge","message":"**Reproducer**\ntools/snapshot/scenes/NotchGlass.hx, top row: the concave-top dropdown.\n\n**Cause**\nsdNotch joined each concave flare to the body with smin. A flare's top edge lies along the body's, so the two distances are equal along that shared edge, and smin bulges the surface there by k/4, with a step where the flare ends inside the body. Liquid glass refracts along the distance's gradient, so the step shows as a bright sliver. Fills and borders hid it, being under a pixel.\n\n**Fix**\nJoin flares with a plain min. The flare's curve meets the body's side tangentially, so nothing is lost.\n\n**Not defects**\n- A flare's interior shows a diagonal crease: a thin wedge's two faces bend light from two sides.\n- A peak narrower than the rim refracts across its whole width, so it reads as the rim's highlight.\n- Chromatic aberration fringes the edges as set.\n\nblinc_ts's sdf.ts and Blinc's notch shader join flares the same way.","files":null}]}